Package: deecure
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: explains your Linux computer and helps fix it safely
 DeeCure checks your computer and explains what it finds in plain
 English: disk space, memory, CPU, battery health, and system services.
 .
 A small background agent collects data every minute, keeps a short
 history, and runs simple rules that turn the data into findings such as
 "Main disk is almost full". The deecure command shows those findings in
 the terminal, and as JSON for scripts.
 .
 Everything stays on this computer. Nothing is sent anywhere.
